---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {getCollection,render} from 'astro:content';

export async function getStaticPaths(){
  return (await getCollection('projects')).map(entry=>({params:{id:entry.id},props:{entry}}));
}

const {entry}=Astro.props;
const {Content}=await render(entry);
const statusLabels={'Idé':'Planned project','Pågående':'Active pilot','Klart':'Published'};
---
<Base title={entry.data.title+' — Solvinter'}><article class="project"><p class="eyebrow">Projects / {statusLabels[entry.data.status]}</p><h1>{entry.data.title}</h1>{entry.id==='observatory'?<><p>Solvinter Observatory is a planned project for identifying opportunities by combining open data, AI and economic analysis. The observatory is open to a range of applications.</p><h3>Compute Economics</h3><p>The first planned application is Compute Economics: tracking GPU prices, mining revenue and rental markets to identify differences in profitability.</p><p>The project is at the idea stage. Data collection and ongoing monitoring are not yet operational.</p></>:entry.id==='eira'?<><p>Eira is a guided AI companion for learning by doing: understanding an assignment, asking questions, solving one problem at a time and reflecting on what comes next.</p><p>A small pilot is underway with participants in Ghana. Participants can suggest improvements, share their needs and help shape the features and ways of working developed next. Their experience and feedback help shape Eira.</p><p>The wider product remains under development, and access is not generally open.</p></>:entry.id==='metabolismx'?<><p>MetabolismX brings together and makes science accessible around one question: what opportunities do people have to influence their health and ageing?</p><p>It focuses on metabolism, longevity and biotechnological advances, and what research could mean for human agency today and in the future.</p><p>The project is already online. An upcoming campaign is being prepared and has not yet launched.</p><p><a href='https://metabolismx.com'>Visit MetabolismX ↗</a></p></>:entry.id==='philosophy-science'?<><p>Essays and reflections on the philosophy of science, nosology, aesthetics, language and logic, ethics, epistemology and metaphysics will be published here.</p><p>The writing explores how we form concepts, what we can know and how our ways of describing the world shape our understanding and actions.</p><p>The first publication is being prepared.</p></>:<Content/>}<a href="/en/#projects">← All projects</a></article></Base>
